// An owned, domain-carrying `[u8; N]` field store admits ONLY a bare string
// literal. Any other expression on the right declines silently, with no
// diagnostic. Reduced from three samples that share this one cause:
// `cli/basics/text_greeting`, `cli/systems/status_report`,
// `cli/text/string_catalog`.
//
//   self.greeting = "Hello, Ada!";          checks
//   self.greeting = ("Hello, Ada!");        checks   (parens are transparent)
//   self.greeting = "Hello, " + "Ada!";     OMITTED  (this fixture)
//   self.greeting = "Hello, " + self.name;  OMITTED
//   self.greeting = self.name;              OMITTED  (a plain copy, no `+`)
//
// Two ADJACENT LITERALS are enough -- there is no runtime operand and no field
// read, and the compiler does not fold `"a" + "b"` into a single String node.
// A carrier-to-carrier copy with no concatenation at all omits too, so this is
// not about concatenation either: the store admits the String node and nothing
// else.
//
// The decline is the `let ... else { return None; }` at
// `psi/pipeline/04_typed-trees-to-checked-trees/src/execution/terminal_unit/
// structural_scalar_store/byte_stores.rs`, where `field_store` requires
// `ExpressionNode::String`. That function sets no `trace.phase` of its own, so
// the label reports the phase entered just before the call and names the ROUTE,
// not the decliner.
//
// Ruled out, each against its control: the `Utf8` DOMAIN shell (a domained
// carrier with a literal checks -- the domain is what puts the store on this
// route, not what declines it; a plain `[u8; N]` never reaches this route and
// omits at `structural field store: scalar field type` for a literal too);
// CAPACITY and array length (8, 16 and 32 behave alike, and a literal that
// genuinely overflows produces a proper diagnostic rather than an omission);
// OPERAND COUNT (two and three operands omit alike); a RUNTIME operand (two
// literals suffice); NESTED carrier paths (`self.catalog.label` behaves as
// `self.greeting` does); and WHERE the store sits (entry body, a sub-state, and
// a separate callee machine all decline at the same site).
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT A GUARD TO LIFT, established by enumeration rather than
// impression. Terminal has exactly three byte-sequence store plans and none
// of them can carry a runtime whole-sequence source:
//
//   ByteSequenceWrite                        one byte at an index, through a
//                                            borrowed view
//   StructuralByteSequenceFieldByteStore     one byte at an index, into a
//                                            field
//   StructuralByteSequenceFieldStore         the whole sequence -- and its
//                                            payload is `bytes: Vec<u8>`, a
//                                            COMPILE-TIME CONSTANT
//
// So the `ExpressionNode::String` requirement in `byte_stores.rs` is not a
// conservative gate in front of a working route; it is the only expression
// the one whole-sequence plan can represent. Deleting it would leave nothing
// to put in `bytes`.
//
// The shape of the repair is already in the codebase, one level down. The
// two single-byte plans carry `value: CheckedByteSequenceStoreValue`, an
// enum that distinguishes a pure expression from a call result. The
// whole-sequence plan needs the same treatment -- a source that is either a
// literal or a carrier place -- and then the codec, stage 05 lowering and
// Omega realization for that new source. That is a cross-stage change, which
// is why this is filed rather than fixed, but it is a vocabulary widening
// with an existing precedent, not an open design question.
//
// MEASUREMENT HAZARD, and the reason this fixture keeps a `write_line` it does
// not otherwise need: A MACHINE WITH NO TERMINAL EFFECT DEMANDS NO UNIT PLAN,
// so every check of it is VACUOUSLY GREEN. The exact body above, stripped of
// its `Binding<Console>`, its `reaches Console` and its console call, CHECKS --
// while the same body with the effect restored omits. A reduction in this area
// that drops the effect while shrinking measures nothing and will report a
// repair that has not happened.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

domain [u8; 32]::Utf8
requires
    valid_utf8(self);

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    greeting: [u8; 32] in Utf8;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    self.greeting = "Hello, " + "Ada!";
    self.console.write_line("done");
}
